<Programs Use="Context">
<Program Use="Context" Name="InstructionSamples">
<Routines Use="Context">
<Routine Use="Context" Name="P_E300Ovld">
<RLLContent Use="Context">
<Rung Use="Target" Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_E300Ovld:  PROCESS -- E300 Overload Relay on EtherNet/IP
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V3.1-00  2014-07-18:  Initial Release (Part of Library of Process Objects V3.1, so Major = 3).
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Using P_Alarm V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.

This Instruction controls and monitors a 193-ECM-ETR (E300
on EtherNet/IP) Overload Relay and provides:

*  Monitoring of warning of impending overloads
*  Ideitification of overload trip conditions
*  Countdown of time until overload trip can be reset
*  Configurable command to initiate a remote test trip
*  Configurable command to initiate a trip reset
NOTE: 3 trips within a configurable time requires resetting the trip LOCALLY (at the relay)!
*  Monitoring of states of relay's discrete inputs and discrete outputs
*  Monitoring of various current, voltage and ground fault values (if available)
*  Monitoring of I/O communication faults
*  Alarms for Trip Warning, Overload Trip and I/O Fault
*  Supports HMI "breadcrumbs" for Alarm Inhibited, Bad Configuration, Not Ready

============================================================
REQUIRED OVERLOAD CONFIGURATION
============================================================
Be certain to set up the E300 Datalinks as follows!
'User Choice' Datalinks are not used by this AOI and
may be left unused or set up for your application.

INPUT ASSEMBLY:
Drive Status (standard)
Feedback (standard)
0. Time to Reset  (Par 3)
1. Time to Start  (Par 31)
2. Trip History #0  (Par 127)
3. Warning History #0  (Par 133)
4. Invalid Configuration Parameter Number  (Par 38)
5. User choice #1
6. User choice #2
7. User choice #3

OUTPUT ASSEMB:Y
This instruction only uses the Remote Trip and Remote Trip Reset command bits in the output assembly.

Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes (Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand) are not used]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[COP(E300_P182:I,P182_Ovld_I,1) ,P_E300Ovld(P182_Ovld,P182_Ovld_I,E300_TripCodeList,E300_WarningCodeList) ,XIC(P182_Ovld.Out_TripReset) OTE(E300_P182:O.TripReset) ,XIC(P182_Ovld.Out_RemoteTrip) OTE(E300_P182:O.RemoteTrip) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
</Controller>
